join Barb left
join Lizzy right
Barb: Um, what the hell is this?
Lizzy: It looks like… a piece of glittery beef jerky.
VO: Now I’m hungry.
Barb: Oooh my god. It’s one of his contraptions.

Lizzy: His "contraptions"?
Barb: You know him and his whacky inventions or whatever. He was probably planning something to ruin grad.
Lizzy: What does the beef jerky have to do with anything?
Barb: It’s not beef jerky, Lizzy. Ugh, you’re such a dog.
Lizzy: Hey!
Barb: It looks like the sorry remains of a ....... belt.
Barb: The structural integrity of faux leather is weaker compared to the high quality of genuine leather.
Barb: but he must’ve cheaped out. Just goes to show that the real thing is worth the money.
